ll, movement on heating-oil costs, or fallout from LePage's Florida residency questions could tip a race this close in either direction.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Open seat: Jared Golden (D) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Maine's second district is a genuine tossup now that Jared Golden has retired, leaving Democrat Matt Dunlap and former governor Paul LePage to compete for an open seat in territory that leans Republican by about four points. Recent surveys give Dunlap a narrow edge — a mid-October poll showed him up four, and an independent University of New Hampshire poll in September had him up six — but most of that polling comes from Democratic sponsors and the pool of credible data is thin.\n\nOutside the polls, the signals tilt the other way. Five of ten expert raters call the race Lean Republican for a flip, three call it a tossup, and only two lean Democratic. Prediction markets put Dunlap's chances in the low-to-mid forties, and LePage holds a fundraising and cash advantage along with decades of name recognition here. The race therefore sits on a hairline Republican edge, with wide uncertainty about which way it breaks.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.4239, "margin": -1.15}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.38, "margin": -2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.3812, "margin": -2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.377, "margin": -2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.3179, "margin": -2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.4062, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.4214, "margin": -1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.437, "margin": -1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.4556, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.4353, "margin": -1.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.4338, "margin": -1.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.4042, "margin": -2.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.4713, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.3776, "margin": -1.5}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "